<%--
Totp_Enrollment

The authenticator-app enrollment ceremony, start to finish, in one component:

    <Totp_Enrollment />

Drop it wherever the enrollment belongs and listen for 'enrolled'. It fetches its own
seed on load, shows the QR code and the manual-entry secret, takes the 6-digit proof (one
digit per box - <Code_Input>, with the cursor already in it), and
then reveals the recovery codes ONCE - which is the only time those codes exist anywhere.
On a deployment that issues no recovery codes (rsx.two_factor.recovery_codes false) there
is no reveal: 'enrolled' fires the moment the proof is accepted.

LAYOUT-NEUTRAL BY CONTRACT. It draws no card, no border and no page heading: the host page
owns the box around it. That is what lets the same component sit in a settings panel, in a
modal and on a sign-in step of the application's own without three variants of itself.

THREE STATES, in the order the template tests them:
  data.setup === null    the seed has not landed yet          -> a loading notice
  state.recovery_codes   the factor is CONFIRMED and the codes
                         are on screen for the only time      -> the reveal
  otherwise              the QR code, the secret, the proof   -> the enrollment form

Args:
  $unstyled_controls - drop the theme (Bootstrap) classes from every control; each keeps its
                 own __ class (see CONTROLS), and the host supplies the whole appearance.
                 The digit boxes are <Code_Input>'s and keep its classes - each box carries
                 Code_Input__box, so the host styles them by that.

No other. The component always enrolls the signed-in identity - the server offers no other
spelling, deliberately (Rsx_Two_Factor_Abstract::__enrolling_identity). On a portal page it
enrolls the signed-in PORTAL user, through the portal realm's controller.

Events:
  enrolled  - fired when the user acknowledges the recovery codes, or as soon as the
              proof is accepted when no sheet was minted. The factor is already live at
              that point; this says the ceremony has nothing more to show.

CONTROLS. Every control carries its own class - Totp_Enrollment__confirm,
Totp_Enrollment__acknowledge, Totp_Enrollment__copy - so a host restyles it by name, never
by a theme class or its position.

See: php artisan rsx:man two_factor
--%>
<Define:Totp_Enrollment tag="div">
    <%
        // $unstyled_controls drops the theme (Bootstrap) classes from every control, leaving
        // each with its own __ class only, for a host whose realm has its own look.
        const _btn = (kind) => (this.args.unstyled_controls ? '' : 'btn btn-' + kind + ' ');
        const _input = this.args.unstyled_controls ? '' : 'form-control ';
    %>
    <% if (!this.data.setup) { %>
        <div class="Totp_Enrollment__notice">Preparing your authenticator setup...</div>
    <% } else if (this.state.recovery_codes) { %>
        <div class="Totp_Enrollment__reveal">
            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__reveal-title">Save your recovery codes</div>
            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__reveal-body">
                Each code signs you in once if you lose your authenticator app. This is the only
                time they are shown.
            </div>

            <ul class="Totp_Enrollment__codes">
                <% for (const code of this.state.recovery_codes) { %>
                    <li class="Totp_Enrollment__code"><%= code %></li>
                <% } %>
            </ul>

            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__actions">
                <button type="button" class="<%= _btn('outline-secondary') %>Totp_Enrollment__copy" $sid="copy">
                    <%= this.state.copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy codes' %>
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="<%= _btn('primary') %>Totp_Enrollment__acknowledge" $sid="acknowledge">I have saved these</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    <% } else { %>
        <div class="Totp_Enrollment__setup">
            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__step">
                Scan this code with your authenticator app, then enter the 6-digit code it shows.
            </div>

            <%-- The server renders the QR as an inline SVG document, so it is interpolated raw
                 rather than served as an <img src>: no second request, nothing cacheable, and
                 the seed never appears in a URL. --%>
            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__qr"><%!= this.data.setup.qr_svg %></div>

            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__manual">
                <span class="Totp_Enrollment__manual-label">Or enter this key manually</span>
                <code class="Totp_Enrollment__secret"><%= this.data.setup.secret %></code>
            </div>

            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__proof">
                <Code_Input $sid="code" $name="code" $align="center" />
            </div>

            <% if (this.state.error) { %>
                <div class="Totp_Enrollment__error"><%= this.state.error %></div>
            <% } %>

            <div class="Totp_Enrollment__actions">
                <button type="button" class="<%= _btn('primary') %>Totp_Enrollment__confirm" $sid="confirm">Confirm</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    <% } %>
</Define:Totp_Enrollment>
